# London nitrogen dioxide: a contour map of 2025 annual mean NO2 at
# 71 continuous monitoring sites (13 AURN, 58 locally managed).
#
# Values: annual mean NO2 (micrograms per cubic metre) from Defra UK-AIR's
#   annual summary files summary_annual_AURN_2025.rds and
#   summary_annual_LMAM_2025.rds, with site locations from
#   AURN_metadata.RData and LMAM_metadata.RData, downloaded 18 November
#   2026 from https://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/openair/R_data/ and
#   https://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/openair/LMAM/R_data/ .
#   Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra).
#   Locally managed (LMAM) sites are run by London boroughs and other
#   networks (London Air Quality Network, Heathrow Airwatch) and are
#   distributed by Defra through UK-AIR.
# Licence: (c) Crown copyright 2026 Defra via uk-air.defra.gov.uk,
#   licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
# Outline: London boroughs, ONS Local Authority Districts (December 2024)
#   BFE; river: OS Open Rivers. Source: Office for National Statistics
#   licensed under the OGL v3.0. Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and
#   database right 2024-2026.
#
# Selection: sites with an annual NO2 mean and at least 75% data capture
# inside the map window (which reaches a little beyond Greater London).
# Roadside, kerbside and background sites are mixed, as published: local
# peaks mark busy roads (e.g. Brixton Road), not a city-wide surface.
# Sites are ordered north to south. Latitude and longitude are converted
# to British National Grid with pyproj (Helmert, within a few metres).
# The outline is the union of the boroughs simplified to 150 m; the
# Thames is the OS Open Rivers route simplified to 60 m.
# Coordinates are kilometres: down from northing 202 km, across from
# easting 502.5 km; 0.2 inch per km.
